From bc85dc8fb3f72e9724d138da19669366dfd11e5a Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ayoub Zaki <ayoub.zaki@embetrix.com>
Date: Mon, 13 Apr 2026 13:45:16 +0200
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] security/keys: add rpi firmware crypto trusted key source

Add a new trusted key source "rpifwcrypto" that uses the Raspberry Pi
VideoCore firmware OTP-backed HMAC-SHA256 to seal and unseal trusted key
material. The OTP key is device-unique and never exported from the
firmware and only the HMAC output is used to derive an AES-256-GCM wrapping
key per-seal binding blobs to the originating device.

Blob layout: header (magic, key_id, nonce, iv, key_len) followed by
AES-256-GCM ciphertext and a 16-byte authentication tag. The header
is included as AAD, so any tampering with key_id, nonce, iv, or
key_len is detected at unseal time.

This is analog to the DCP trusted key source: a hardware-bound wrapping
key derived from a firmware/hardware KDF with software
AES-GCM for the actual key material wrap.
Keys are non-migratable (migratable=0) as they are bound to the device OTP.

Signed-off-by: Ayoub Zaki <ayoub.zaki@embetrix.com>
