+Trusted Keys usage: RPi firmware crypto
+----------------------------------------
+
+Prerequisites:
+
+* A Raspberry Pi SoC with VideoCore firmware that supports the OTP crypto
+  mailbox tags (``0x0003008f`` / ``0x00030092``).
+* The target OTP key slot must be programmed (non-zero) before use.
+  A slot with all-zero content causes the firmware to return an error.
+
+Key slot 1 is used by default. Override with ``trusted.rpifwcrypto_key_id=N``
+if a different slot is needed.
+
+Usage::
+
+    keyctl add trusted name "new keylen" ring
+    keyctl add trusted name "load hex_blob" ring
+    keyctl print keyid
+
+"keyctl print" returns an ASCII hex copy of the sealed key, which is in format
+specific to this rpifwcrypto key-blob implementation. The key length for new keys is
+always in bytes. Trusted Keys can be 32 - 128 bytes (256 - 1024 bits).
+
 Encrypted Keys usage
 --------------------
 
